  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of powers of two motors is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;that are capable of raising&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;water in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;minutes and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;water in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;minutes respectively from a well of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;deep. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The work done in raising the water is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>h</mi></math>.</p><p>Power is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>t</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>Let the powers of both the motors be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;respectively.</p><p>Hence, the ratio of the powers is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>300</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>25</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}